<title>USA: NYSE Unavailables -.</title>
<headline>NYSE Unavailables -.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New York Stock Exchange said Wednesday AMP Inc, Integon Corp and Applied Magnetics Corp were not available for after-hours trading for news.  </p>
<p>The three companies released their quarterly earnings earlier in the day.</p>
<p>The exchange said Mid-American Waste preferred A stock, Eljer Industries, Corimon SACA, Westmoreland Coal Co and Westmoreland preferred A stock were also unavailable for trading.</p>
<p>The exchange announced earlier in the day it was going to delist Eljer's stock, explaining how fewer than 600,000 of he company's common shares were held by the public.</p>
